  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 204 PM MDT Thu Oct 1 2026\n\nMostly benign and warm conditions expected as we move into the\nlong term starting with Sunday, which will actually be our \ncoolest day of the period. We'll see widespread temperatures in\nthe 70's with a few sites possibly peaking around 80, but Monday\ninto Tuesday more widespread upper 70's to 80's will be present\nunder high pressure ridging. This feature may briefly recede\nand flatten thanks to troughing to the north and allow for a bit\nmore widespread 70's to return by the end of the forecast\nperiod, but this will likely be brief as extended models show \nthe ridge building back in beyond the long term. Otherwise with \nno major features expected to add variability to the forecast, \npressure gradients will remain on the weak side with a chance \nat daily breezy, diurnally driven winds, but nowhere near strong\nfor this region. Elevated to near critical fire weather \nconditions could be present thanks to the expected dryness and \nthe afternoon breezy winds, and will need to be monitored \nparticularly on Monday when RH's look to be at their lowest. \nOverall there is high confidence in the forecast, with ensembles\nshowing near unanimous agreement on the above forecast, as a\nwarm start to fall and October continues.",
